<priority_guidelines>
Priority guidelines:
Be EXTREMELY selective with "high" priority. Reserve "high" priority ONLY for:
- Critical issues requiring immediate attention (e.g., campaign failing, budget exhausted early, zero conversions)
- Exceptional opportunities that demand urgent action (e.g., unexpectedly high ROAS, viral performance)
- Severe underperformance or overspending that threatens campaign success

Most findings should be "low" priority. Use "high" sparingly - only when the finding represents a truly urgent, business-critical situation.

It is perfectly acceptable to return an empty array [] if nothing notable or actionable stands out from the data. Do not generate findings for the sake of having findings.
</priority_guidelines>
